# Files NOT uploaded to Vercel.
#
# vercel.json blocks build/meta trees with a hand-maintained REDIRECT list
# (/docs/*, /tools/*, /.claude/*, ...). That list drifts: every new top-level
# directory is publicly served until someone remembers to add a rule — /tests/*
# was already exposed that way, and the native-app work added android/, ios/ and
# app/. This file is the deny-by-default complement: excluded paths are never
# uploaded, so they cannot be served at all.
#
# ⚠ DO NOT exclude api/ or lib/ — the serverless functions are api/*.js and they
# import from lib/ at runtime. Everything below is build-, docs- or app-only.

# Native app projects and the generated web bundle (can contain signing config)
android/
ios/
app/

# App toolchain. The serverless functions import ONLY Node built-ins (verified:
# no bare npm imports in api/ or lib/), so the site needs no npm install. Keeping
# package.json out of the upload also preserves Vercel's existing build detection
# for the website, which had no root package.json before the app work.
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json
capacitor.config.json

# Build scripts, tests, and internal docs — never served
tools/
tests/
docs/
.claude/
.github/

# Local secrets (belt and braces; also git-ignored)
revenuecat.json
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
